# Committed on purpose — see .gitignore, which carves out an exception for
# this file the same way it does for .env.example.
#
# Both values below are NEXT_PUBLIC_* by necessity: Next.js inlines them into
# the client bundle at build time, so they are visible to anyone who views
# the page source regardless of where they are set. There is nothing to leak.
#
# This file exists because NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is required at BUILD time —
# not runtime — and the host's environment-variable panel may only inject
# variables into the already-running process, never into the build step
# itself. `next build` reads .env.production automatically and unconditionally,
# so committing the real values here works regardless of how the host wires
# its UI, and removes one more way this can silently ship broken.
#
# If the canonical URL is ever wrong on the live site again, check here first.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://bracketsight.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT=ca-pub-1973018352310576
